# Data layer and data policy

- All content flows through the `ContentRepository` interface exported from `@/lib/content`. Pages, components, the terminal snapshot, the sitemap and the admin never import Sanity (`@sanity/*`, `src/lib/content/sanity/*`) directly; ESLint enforces it.
- Two adapters, `sanity` and `fixtures`, pass the same contract tests. zod schemas in `src/lib/content/schema.ts` are the single contract; types are `z.infer` of them.
- Reads skip and log invalid documents; writes reject with field-level errors. Hidden items (`visible: false`) never reach any public output (HTML, sitemap, terminal, JSON-LD). The phone number never appears in metadata, structured data or the terminal.
- Sanity is contacted only from the server. Reads use `fetch` with `next: { tags }` (`content:*` tags); writes use `updateTag` plus `revalidatePath` for affected routes.
- Data policy: all seed content is fictional (invented companies, people and metrics, `example.com` URLs) and flagged `isFixture: true`. The only real facts are the owner's name, job title and city in `src/config/site.ts`. Never present anything as a real claim about the owner. No lorem ipsum, no TODO in rendered text.
